    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith the overlap scheduler, after `forward_batch_generation` returns for a non-speculative batch, the scheduler calls `self.future_map.publish(future_indices, batch.seq_lens + 1)`. That call writes `FutureMap.new_seq_lens_buf`, but only two places read that buffer:\n\n- `FutureMap.resolve_seq_lens_cpu`, which returns early when `batch.spec_info is None`;\n- `FutureMap.resolve_mixed_spec_tails`, which only runs for speculative batches.\n\nFor non-speculative batches `publish` records no event and receives no confidence tensor here. Each decode step therefore launches two kernels on the forward stream, `seq_lens + 1` and the scatter, and nothing reads the result.\n\n## Modifications\n\nRemove the non-speculative `publish` call and the comment line that described it. Speculative batches still publish through `on_publish` from inside the worker.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOverlap scheduling on an out-of-tree platform: non-speculative in eager and graph mode, speculative in graph mode. Non-speculative outputs match the golden tokens. GSM8K stays within baseline noise: 0.8832 against 0.8875 +/- 0.0107 without speculative decoding, and 0.9469 against 0.952 +/- 0.0107 with it.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting: black-stable (ruff-format compatible).\n- [ ] Unit tests: none added; happy to add one if wanted.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40976085063](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40976085063)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40976084832](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40976084832)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40976085130](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40976085130)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
